Mainnet database findings
public.dapp_service_requests currently permits only pi_studio and developer.
The dApp request tables have RLS enabled; there are no client policies for dapp_service_requests, and direct table grants are limited to postgres/service_role. Do not broaden those grants or add client policies for this feature.
Mainnet public.projects currently has one eligible-looking registry row for this scope: MAITAGOGO TABLE WATER, type internal, status approved. Its owner_albukhr_user_id resolves to public.users and an active Contributor mapping. Its legacy owner_user_id is NULL.
There are no active rows in albukhr_security.project_user_bindings currently.
Three External Project applications exist in statuses draft, needs_revision, and submitted; none is converted into public.projects. They must not be advertised as registered External Projects.
albukhr_security.project_user_bindings.role is restricted to internal_manager / external_manager; a binding is active only when active=true, revoked_at IS NULL, and revoked_by IS NULL.
3. Eligibility resolver contract
Add a Mainnet-only authenticated endpoint:
GET /api/dapp-service/v2/projects/eligible
The gateway must authenticate the Pi access token through the existing Pi /v2/me flow and take the UID only from that trusted response. Never accept pi_uid, network, owner ID, relationship, project type or project name as trusted authority from the browser.
Resolution algorithm
Resolve exactly one public.users record by the verified pi_uid and network='mainnet'. If none exists, return an empty project list; do not attempt fuzzy username matching.
List registered public.projects rows only where network='mainnet', project_type IN ('internal','external'), and status is not suspended or archived. Only actual rows in public.projects qualify; an External application row is not itself a registered project.
Record relationship owner only when the verified public.users.id exactly matches projects.owner_albukhr_user_id. Where a verified active Contributor mapping links this public user ID to an Auth UID, a matching projects.owner_user_id may also prove legacy ownership.
Record relationship manager only when the verified public user maps through albukhr_security.contributors.albukhr_user_id -> contributors.user_id, and an active, non-revoked project_user_bindings row for that Auth UID and project has the role corresponding to the project type (internal_manager or external_manager). If the identity bridge is absent, do not infer a manager relationship.
Never use core_admin_bindings to grant project eligibility. Never return core projects. Never infer ownership from matching names, usernames, business names or client payload.
Return only safe selection fields: id, project_code, name, project_type, status, relationship. The project name and type shown are database-derived.
Suggested response:
{
  "success": true,
  "network": "mainnet",
  "projects": [
    {
      "id": "<uuid>",
      "project_code": "<database project code>",
      "name": "<database project name>",
      "project_type": "internal",
      "status": "approved",
      "relationship": "owner"
    }
  ]
}
4. Request submission rules
Extend the existing POST /requests in a backward-compatible way.
pi_studio and developer: preserve current required fields and behavior; new project-context fields remain NULL.
albukhr_project: require a valid projectId; run the eligibility resolver again at submission time; reject if the project is not currently eligible for that verified Pi UID.
For albukhr_project, derive project_name, project_type, and project_relationship from the database and resolver. Never trust a client-supplied projectName or relationship value to identify the project.
Set request status to submitted, payment status to unpaid, and network to the server-fixed mainnet, as the existing gateway does.
Preserve the existing consent version validation and no-store response headers.
Do not create a quote, payment intent, or payment confirmation during submission.
5. Database migration draft
Apply DAPP_SERVICE_PROJECT_ELIGIBILITY_MIGRATION_DRAFT.sql only after explicit approval and after reviewing it against the latest live schema. It proposes nullable project_id, project_type, and project_relationship fields, a restrictive FK to public.projects, an additive albukhr_project service-type value, a context constraint, and an index. It does not touch RLS policies, grants, payment tables, Admin roles, network switching or existing request rows.
6. User-side UI
Add the third service option with machine value albukhr_project and display label “Build an App for My ALBUKHR Project”.
Selecting it reveals a required project selector populated only by GET /projects/eligible.
Show each choice with project name, type, code and verified relationship.
If no eligible project is returned, show an explanatory message and links to the existing External Project dashboard/registration flow; do not manufacture an eligibility record.
Selecting either existing service hides/clears the project selector and follows its current path unchanged.
Keep the existing Pi auth core, environment core, and Mainnet-only behavior. No LocalStorage/sessionStorage state for eligibility.
7. Admin queue changes
Extend queue/detail API projections and Admin UI to display:
request service type (human-readable label for albukhr_project),
project name and project ID,
project type (internal / external),
server-verified relationship (owner / manager).
Show these fields only when the request is for albukhr_project. Existing queue filtering, transitions, quote workflow, MFA/AAL2 checks, and payment handling remain unchanged. Do not let Admin UI-supplied relationship fields affect authorization; they are display snapshots written by the trusted gateway.
8. Required regression/security checks
pi_studio submission still succeeds with old payload; project fields stay NULL.
developer submission still succeeds with old payload; project fields stay NULL.
albukhr_project without projectId fails safely.
A forged project name or relationship is ignored; names/type/relationship are derived server-side.
A Core project ID is rejected even if posted directly.
A project owned by a different Pi UID is rejected.
An arbitrary External application ID is rejected; only a registry project in public.projects can qualify.
Suspended/archived projects are excluded. Mainnet resolver never returns Testnet rows.
Revoked/inactive manager bindings are rejected; only matching typed active bindings qualify.
If user -> Auth UID bridge is missing, manager eligibility fails closed; direct owner_albukhr_user_id owner check still works.
Admin queue shows project ID/type/relationship for project requests and does not expose another applicant's private data.
Existing quote, status transition, request history and payment paths are unchanged.
Verify API DAPP_SERVICE_V2_ENABLED=false and Pi payments remain disabled throughout this draft stage.
9. Rollout boundaries
This is a draft only. No SQL writes, GitHub changes, deployment, Storage modifications, real Pi payments, or production enabling were performed. Next implementation work should be an additive patch set for the User HTML/JS, API gateway, Admin queue HTML/JS and a migration file; after review, tests must run in isolated fixtures before any production change is considered.
